<h3>Pre-loading Protocols</h3>

<p>To ensure a safe and secure transportation process, follow these actionable checklist points:</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>360-Degree Digital Condition Audit:</strong> Before initiating the transportation process, conduct a thorough digital condition audit of the two-wheeler or motorcycle. Document every aspect, including the wheels, engine, exhaust, fuel tank, lighting system, and accessories.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Battery Terminal Checks:</strong> Perform a battery terminal check to ensure the bike's electrical system is in good condition. Check the battery connections, charging system, and cables to prevent any potential issues during transit.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>One-Quarter Tank Fuel Regulation:</strong> Maintain the bike with one-quarter tank fuel to avoid spillage during transportation and unnecessary weight on the vehicle. Aim for a balanced weight distribution for a smooth ride.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Fastag Management:</strong> To simplify the journey on Indian highways, manage your Fastag account efficiently. Fastag is an electronic toll collection system that allows seamless movement on national highways.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Transportation via Train:</strong> For those utilizing bike transport via train, follow these steps:</span></li>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Booking Train Tickets:</strong> Book your train tickets in advance to secure a confirmed berth for your motorcycle. Contact the train reservation centers or visit the official IRCTC website for guidance.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Preparing the Motorcycle:</strong> Clean the motorcycle thoroughly before transport to prevent dirt or grime from damaging the vehicle or causing inconvenience during loading and unloading.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Working with Packers and Movers:</strong> If you choose to work with packers and movers, ensure they have experience in transporting motorcycles and follow the mentioned protocols.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Documentation:</strong> Obtain necessary documentation like the Vehicle Registration Certificate (Form 26) or the showroom invoice to facilitate the transportation process.</span></li>
